  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If you leave the game, the cards remain exiled face down indefinitely. No player may look at them.",
      "oracle_id": "5513a221-dfff-4e02-8037-dcff3d0381d7",
      "published_at": "2024-07-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once an Assassin creature or commander you control deals combat damage to a player in a turn, you can cast spells for their freerunning costs for the rest of that turn. It doesn’t matter what happens to that Assassin or commander after that.",
      "oracle_id": "5513a221-dfff-4e02-8037-dcff3d0381d7",
      "published_at": "2024-07-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You pay all costs and follow all normal timing rules for cards played this way. For example, if one of the exiled cards is a land card, you may play it only during your main phase while the stack is empty.",
      "oracle_id": "5513a221-dfff-4e02-8037-dcff3d0381d7",
      "published_at": "2024-07-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Effects that instruct you to reveal or look at cards from the top of you library will still work. Only effects that use the word \"search\" are affected.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect says \"Search your library . . . then shuffle your library,\" you shuffle you libraries even though you can't search.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect says \"You may search your library . . . If you do, shuffle your library\" or \"You may search your library . . . then shuffle your library,\" you can't choose to search, so you won't shuffle.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The only difference between a colored artifact and a colorless artifact is, obviously, its color. Unlike most artifacts, a colored artifact requires colored mana to cast. Also unlike most artifacts, a colored artifact has a color in all zones. It will interact with cards that care about color. Other than that, a colored artifact behaves just like any other artifact. It will interact as normal with any card that cares about artifacts, such as Shatter or Arcbound Ravager.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is now targeted.",
      "oracle_id": "57f90b30-bcb0-447e-8788-5c5ded187207",
      "published_at": "2007-07-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.",
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2004-12-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".",
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Cycling is an activated ability. Effects that interact with activated abilities (such as Stifle or Rings of Brighthearth) will interact with cycling. Effects that interact with spells (such as Remove Soul or Faerie Tauntings) will not.",
      "oracle_id": "79d290ea-c095-4135-9711-f3ce089dae43",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target player for Jace's last ability has no cards in hand, that player shuffles nothing into their library, and that player's library will remain empty. That player won't lose the game until they try to draw from the empty library.",
      "oracle_id": "7f77a84e-5a4b-4834-aefa-3cecc175ae8e",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You draw three cards and put two cards back all while Jace's second ability is resolving. Nothing can happen between the two, and no player may choose to take actions.",
      "oracle_id": "7f77a84e-5a4b-4834-aefa-3cecc175ae8e",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Follow the instructions in the order listed on the card: if you target yourself, you'll put the top two cards of your library into your graveyard and then draw a card.",
      "oracle_id": "83101ba8-a569-4827-8c53-9ca0dfcd59a7",
      "published_at": "2011-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target player is an illegal target when Thought Scour tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card.",
      "oracle_id": "83101ba8-a569-4827-8c53-9ca0dfcd59a7",
      "published_at": "2011-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": " \"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": " A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": " If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": " To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": " You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": " You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Only you get to look at the exiled card. Its owner doesn't get to know what it is while it is in exile unless you tell them.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You don't have to disclose which card you exiled and which card you put on the bottom of the library. For example, if your opponent knows what the top card of their library is and you cast Siphon Insight, you don't have to tell them where you put that card.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may play the card even if it is a land.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow all normal timing rules to play a card exiled with Siphon Insight.",
      "oracle_id": "aee82122-d13e-4175-b499-9dde718e4da9",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After the search is complete, the entire library is shuffled.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each search works exactly the same as normal except that the opponent doing the searching sees only the top four cards of that library. They can't look at the other cards in that library at all. Cards not in the top four cards of the library can't be found in the search, even if they're identifiable in some manner.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For effects that check whether a player searched a library or may search a library, searching the top four cards of that library counts as searching that library.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect uses the word \"search\" once but allows an opponent to search for multiple cards, the top four cards remain the same throughout the entire search. Finding one card won't cause the fifth card to become included in the search.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This does not cause a player to lose if they have less than 3 cards in their library. It allows you to look at and reorder or shuffle whatever remaining cards there might be.",
      "oracle_id": "e744dbb6-2d56-462a-8d49-d79c73944048",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
